      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Forced Near Distance overrides the world’s ref camera, which can result in a complete breakdown of a world’s skybox geometry which is sometimes necessary to use for shader reasons and because the regular Unity skybox doesnt work correctly for distant (>30km) scenery in Unity 2022. Forced Near Distance being applied in worlds where it is not useful can also lead to other issues that break long sight lines, dramatically amplify apparent jitter in UI elements and other geometry much closer to origin than normal, and distort or hide geometry. I’ve never heard if it causing the client to become unstable, but I’m not surprised given the way it was implemented.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
